      "text": "Low experiential fidelity occurs when a free roaming virtual world with endless possibilities leads every usage to a different experience, because that is not what happens in the real world, while higher experiential fidelity results when real-world constraints are placed on virtual navigation, movement, and interaction, making the virtual experience closer to the real world."
