      "evidence": [1, 2, 6, 7],
      "text": "The consistency required by Shneiderman's first golden rule has two types: internal consistency and external or environmental consistency."
    },
    {
      "evidence": [2, 3, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10],
      "text": "Internal consistency in system design means using the same elements and interactions for the same task across different parts of a design and different usage instances, rather than using separate objects, elements, or interactions."
    },
