      "evidence": [3, 6, 7, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15, 16],
      "text": "External or environmental consistency in system design means that the elements and interactions in a virtual world should closely match the user's real-world experience and knowledge, so that real-world knowledge transfers to the virtual world as closely as possible."
    },
    {
      "evidence": [1, 17, 23, 36],
      "text": "Shneiderman's second golden rule is to design for universal usability, meaning a system should provide facilities for all user categories and support different user categories rather than only specific user categories."
