{
  "facts": [
    {
      "evidence": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 13],
      "text": "The seventh usability rule, keeping users in control, requires that lay users feel in control of the system, perceive that their interaction changes the system state, and receive feedback on their actions and results, because lack of this feeling makes them feel at a loss and reduces usability."
