      "text": "The final design of the Majuli virtual reality (VR) tour was developed using the interactive system development lifecycle (ISDL) model, an iterative design-prototype-evaluate cycle that started with a design based on design guidelines and continuously refined design ideas from feedback and observations obtained by involving end users passively or actively."
    },
    {
      "evidence": [9, 27, 28],
      "text": "Initial prototypes for the Majuli virtual reality (VR) tour were influenced by observations of the behaviors and preferences of the island's visitors, who were the potential users, and those observations informed design choices about which locations to cover, how to categorize and identify user groups, and how to integrate cultural videos and navigation features suitable for those user groups."
    },
    {
      "evidence": [9, 29, 30],
      "text": "User feedback and interaction with users for the Majuli virtual reality (VR) tour led to incorporated design elements such as a minimap, a notification system, and user controls."
